    "id": "er2lipfdr_1",
    "stac_version": "1.1.0",
    "description": "The CAMEX-3 ER-2 Lightning Instrument Package (LIP) Ferry and Dry Run data files consists of electrical field measurements of lightning from eight field mills, conductivity probe temperatures from two probes, and navigation data collected using the Lightning Instrument Package (LIP) flown onboard the NASA ER-2 aircraft during ferry and dry run in support of the third field campaign in the Convection And Moisture EXperiment (CAMEX) series, CAMEX-3. This field campaign took place from August to September 1998 based out of Patrick Air Force Base in Florida, with the purpose of studying various aspects of tropical cyclones in the region. The ferry and dry run took place from August 4, 1998 through September 28, 1998. These data are available in HDF-4 file format with browse imagery available in GIF file format.",
